'''''Passiflora subpeltata''''', commonly known as '''white passionflower''', is a [[Passiflora|passion flower]] bearing yellow-green fruits.<ref name=":0">{{Cite web |title=Passiflora subpeltata |url=https://tropical.theferns.info/viewtropical.php?id=Passiflora+subpeltata |access-date=2025-11-01 |website=Useful Tropical Plants}}</ref> It is a vining plant with three-lobed leaves and 2-3 ornate flowers.<ref>{{Cite web |title=Passiflora subpeltata Ortega |url=https://www.worldfloraonline.org/taxon/wfo-0000480121#synonyms |access-date=2025-11-01 |website=The World Flora Online}}</ref> It is grown as an ornamental plant.<ref name=":0" /> This vine is also a marginal pest in areas.

